00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Seven stories from the heart of the Halo universe.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Halo Legends is a animation, war, action film directed by Hiroshi Yamazaki.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
The universe of the Halo video game series is expanded in seven short
animated films from Japan's greatest anime directors and studios.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Female Soldier ("Prototype") / Kelly ("The Package"), played by Luci Christian.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Master Chief, played by David Wald.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Spartan ("The Babysitter"), played by Emily Neves.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Cortana / Dr. Halsey, played by Shelley Calene-Black.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Haka (segment "The Duel"), played by Jessie James Grelle.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Sister (segment "Odd One Out"), played by Brittney Karbowski.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Halo Legends (ヘーローレジェンズ Hērō rejenzu) is a 2010 adult animated military
science fiction anthology film produced by 343 Industries.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The anime compiles seven animated short films, detailing the backstory of the Halo universe, in
addition to providing side stories that expand the universe and tie into the film series.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Following the same pattern that other films such as The Animatrix and Batman: Gotham Knight used, the animated movies were created by six
Japanese anime production houses: Bee Train, Bones, Casio Entertainment, Production I.G., Studio 4°C, and Toei Animation.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Shinji Aramaki, creator and director of Appleseed and Appleseed Ex
Machina, serves as the project's creative advisor.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Warner Bros.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
released Legends on DVD and Blu-ray Disc on February 16, 2010.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The idea for an anime compilation existed for years
before there was momentum for the project.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
343 creative director Frank O'Connor produced story outlines or finished
scripts that the production houses animated in a variety of styles.

18
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:06,000
The film explores themes of anthology, based on video game, anime.

19
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
